    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286">

                <pb facs="0415" n="399" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3231/6–148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Key</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-01T19:00:00-03:00">June 1, 1948—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>602. Lopez Rodriguez of Ministry of Finance inquired re status present US/Brazil
                    reciprocal trade agreement<anchor n="1" xml:id="d286-f1"/> when GATT takes
                    effect. He understands present agreement is not to be denounced but instead is
                    to be suspended while GATT remains in force through exchange of notes. Telegraph
                    action proposed this connection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Key</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
